From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:24:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 133/144] GreatDANE: pin l10n fixtures to the 153.7.0esr
 revision; assert CRLF on the maintenance line (round 4h)

NGD 4f+4g L3 / LOW: the updater.ini fixtures and browser/locales/l10n-changesets.json
are pinned to the 153.7.0esr l10n-changesets revision

    4e2e25a0b94740a84c357e93346ec4f4c94521e3

Every locale in that file records this SHA. The six fixtures fetched at this
revision are byte-identical to the previous 4f pin (3ae91662ee285b44f21ef31b9cae722d132e28ea).
locale_branding_check.py records the full SHA.

The CRLF case now asserts that the MozillaMaintenanceDescription line itself
ends in CRLF, not merely that some CRLF exists in the file (NGD L4 follow-up).

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
